No, the provisions of Michigan’s Truth in Renting Act do not apply to all types of lease agreements. Under MCL 554.632(a), the Truth in Renting Act does not apply if the rental agreement ONLY contains one or more of the following:

(1) The identities of the parties;
(2) A description of the premises;
(3) The rental period;
(4) The total rental amount due;
(5) The amount of rental payments; and
(6) The times at which rental payments are due.
